{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790509060,"nonce":"DJYnMrotDsWLNWUOaRk+zn1i8gU=","title":"AOT hosts cannot add frontend objects to the final link","message":"`emit_aot` accepts a host runtime and typed native links, but it cannot accept relocatable objects produced by another frontend. A multi-language host must prejoin those objects into its runtime before calling Ash. On wasm that duplicates linking work and makes the runtime artifact depend on whichever languages happen to be in one program.\n\nAdd caller-owned relocatable objects to `AotRequest`. They should be passed beside Ash's generated object parts to `link_executable`; successful cleanup must remove only Ash's scratch objects. The CLI supplies an empty list. Caribou's Haxe/Wren fixture is the end-to-end validation: WrenLift's object is an independent input to `ash_wasm_link`, and the resulting program still runs its direct cross-language calls.","files":null}]}